#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063984 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b47545-fdf1-5e6a-b0bb-bbbecb8067cc" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Positive Integer Exponent"}] :question/id #uuid "eff323d1-4e70-5490-8e41-9fbf00c387f5" :question/math-academy-id "e-446" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int (3x+1)^3 \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nu=3x+1\n$$\n\nThen differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u$, calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(3x + 1)^{3}dx &= \\intu^{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\intu^{3}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{u^{4}}{4} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{12}u^{4} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{12}(3x + 1)^{4} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}[\\frac{1}{12}(3x + 1)^{4} + C] &= \\frac{1}{12} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}[(3x + 1)^{4}] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{12} \\cdot 4(3x + 1)^{3} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(3x + 1) + 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}(3x + 1)^{3} \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= (3x + 1)^{3}✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063985 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387d85df-b839-5837-89b9-5e4bb4daa073" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Negative Integer Exponent"}] :question/id #uuid "e469c042-9619-55d4-b745-d4ed26251d80" :question/math-academy-id "e-447" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2}{(1-x)^3} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int 2(1-x)^{-3} \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-x$. Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\textrm d u\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u$, calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int2(1 - x)^{-3}dx &= \\int2u^{-3} \\cdot (-1)du \\\\\n&=-2\\intu^{-3}du \\\\\n&=-2 \\cdot \\frac{u^{-2}}{-2} + C \\\\\n&= u^{-2} + C \\\\\n&= (1 - x)^{-2} + C \\\\\n&= (1)/((1 - x)^{2}) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}[(1)/((1 - x)^{2}) + C] &= \\frac{d}{dx}[(1)/((1 - x)^{2})] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}[(1 - x)^{-2}] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&=-2(1 - x)^{-3} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(1 - x) + 0 \\\\\n&= - (2)/((1 - x)^{3}) \\cdot (-1) \\\\\n&= (2)/((1 - x)^{3})✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063988 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Fractional Exponent"}] :question/id #uuid "e416cb5c-22df-55e4-a3cb-c6b5dfc650c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-448" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int\\sqrt{1-5x}\\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int(1-5x)^{1/2}\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=1-5x$. Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 5 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u$, calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(1 - 5x)^{1/2}dx &= \\intu^{1/2} \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{5}\\intu^{1/2}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15}u^{3/2} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15}(1 - 5x)^{3/2} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(1 - 5x)^{3}} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}[- \\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(1 - 5x)^{3}} + C] &= -\\frac{2}{15} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}[\\sqrt{(1 - 5x)^{3}}] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}[(1 - 5x)^{3/2}] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15} \\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(1 - 5x)^{1/2} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(1 - 5x) + 0 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{5}(1 - 5x)^{1/2} \\cdot (-5) \\\\\n&= (1 - 5x)^{1/2}✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b47545-fdf1-5e6a-b0bb-bbbecb8067cc" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Positive Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1093df55-e4fd-5266-afc9-1e6d00db1da1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255912} {:answer/id #uuid "b4351526-8b5b-5ed4-b769-a21523fe75e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255913} {:answer/id #uuid "b742c578-3187-549e-9786-01d7d8ae97d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255914} {:answer/id #uuid "853fa269-4d94-5236-991b-ce2f8aea2327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255915} {:answer/id #uuid "c2429bef-6706-53fa-881a-7fe58a7d2c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2429bef-6706-53fa-881a-7fe58a7d2c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3x-2)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255916} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d9561b8-1cf3-5d55-859d-8cba3e45b1f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255911}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22b9e6d8-eac2-556d-ac94-c171a6cadf5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-113486" :question/problem "$\\int 48(3x-2)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3x-2.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 48(3x-2)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 48{u}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =48\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =2\\cdot {u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =2(3x-2)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-2)^{8}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-2)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =16(3x-2)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-2)+0 \\\\  & =16(3x-2)^{7}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =48(3x-2)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b47545-fdf1-5e6a-b0bb-bbbecb8067cc" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Positive Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0e08971-039c-5916-9b12-85d583d48e5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255919} {:answer/id #uuid "be58e587-aea9-560e-9a13-cf2848d5db72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255920} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c0e2fa-95ab-521c-827b-53bf52dcdf1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255921} {:answer/id #uuid "07cdebcb-6b52-5c0a-ba32-ef0c743f45ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255922} {:answer/id #uuid "99ff9bea-f0a9-53cd-9159-90d8055b76a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be58e587-aea9-560e-9a13-cf2848d5db72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255920} :answer-field/id #uuid "820a10db-076d-5b88-a7eb-c533067ddf9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255918}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6477ece7-72c1-5377-8b6c-83eda134c6c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-113492" :question/problem "$\\int 6(5-3x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=5-3x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6(5-3x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{u}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\int {u}^{2}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\int {u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{2}{3}(5-3x)^{3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-2(5-3x)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-3x)+0 \\\\  & =-2(5-3x)^{2}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6(5-3x)^{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b47545-fdf1-5e6a-b0bb-bbbecb8067cc" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Positive Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fc0a28b-c5be-5508-9691-bd75643d1f19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255926} {:answer/id #uuid "0f7d115a-40e8-5f9b-86f2-f85333b421fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255927} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3ec2dc-930d-55df-af4b-c9b66f693e80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255928} {:answer/id #uuid "82ef7604-8d9b-5eff-927e-b5ec9885b885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255929} {:answer/id #uuid "c657b13e-8cc1-5158-8fc3-8bc37dd730b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f7d115a-40e8-5f9b-86f2-f85333b421fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255927} :answer-field/id #uuid "be7ae9cd-355c-58e2-9264-80aa13dd39aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255925}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "201b1303-edfe-5a94-b70a-3687fd03d284" :question/math-academy-id "q-113502" :question/problem "$\\int 18(2-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2-5x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 18(2-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 18{u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =18\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\int {u}^{5}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{u}^{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2-5x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{5}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =18(2-5x)^{5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b47545-fdf1-5e6a-b0bb-bbbecb8067cc" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Positive Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ab3379a-f72a-547a-a712-e7549846f133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255933} {:answer/id #uuid "47227283-f02b-5bb5-baf9-c048655d39d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255934} {:answer/id #uuid "4eab4ba4-33d5-5950-a676-292915b674f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255935} {:answer/id #uuid "05b9fad4-f394-5e53-9c49-8d7637653fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255936} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1a0e75-0f67-5010-97f4-32d472064a34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05b9fad4-f394-5e53-9c49-8d7637653fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255936} :answer-field/id #uuid "2445d7bf-bed5-53ac-bf0f-f97b1b775b70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255932}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4f3c217a-2c5a-5d18-9a3f-59edcf917f64" :question/math-academy-id "q-113503" :question/problem "$\\int 9(3-2x)^{8}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3-2x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9(3-2x)^{8}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 9{u}^{8}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\int {u}^{8}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}\\int {u}^{8}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{9}}{9}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{9}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{2}(3-2x)^{9}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}(3-2x)^{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3-2x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}(3-2x)^{8}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =9(3-2x)^{8}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387d85df-b839-5837-89b9-5e4bb4daa073" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Negative Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f034061-faaf-5f2d-8012-9766cef6d43a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255940} {:answer/id #uuid "be3470b9-6a83-5045-9e64-0714b5c203e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255941} {:answer/id #uuid "3771c00f-af07-53e7-984d-3a753a36e261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255942} {:answer/id #uuid "914cc726-ec03-5e57-9563-65a55e62819c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255943} {:answer/id #uuid "fc0fd2d9-a9ef-5a79-99ab-10eb52c2b299" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc0fd2d9-a9ef-5a79-99ab-10eb52c2b299" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255944} :answer-field/id #uuid "aabd1db3-f13d-506c-9d3f-3a5bb1d65253" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255939}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1948aa2d-5fbb-59f5-8ccc-6dd9cfd6ef51" :question/math-academy-id "q-113509" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (x-2)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=x-2.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x-2)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{-3}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{u}^{2}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(x-2)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (x-2)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x-2)+0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387d85df-b839-5837-89b9-5e4bb4daa073" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Negative Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef1a4d19-c649-5a42-b37a-a3cedd37dacc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{35(5x-1)^{7}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255947} {:answer/id #uuid "75e282a3-2331-58cb-b900-7f618ed96fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255948} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3ec94f-a0c6-53c8-8916-938b8ce1d934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5(5x-1)^{7}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255949} {:answer/id #uuid "1130df90-df7c-5f76-839c-4a8178a11de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5(5x-1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255950} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9e0721-472b-538e-8482-f7367d5bfdb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd9e0721-472b-538e-8482-f7367d5bfdb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255951} :answer-field/id #uuid "36c78e2d-d91d-5796-8eb4-d1455c6a7591" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255946}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ae7beff-7f65-5fd8-9a89-d99b8ffa80b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-113511" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{(5x-1)^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (5x-1)^{-6}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5x-1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5x-1)^{-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{-6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{-6}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5}){u}^{-5}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{25{u}^{5}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{25(5x-1)^{5}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{25}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(5x-1)^{-5}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{25}\\cdot (-5)\\cdot (5x-1)^{-6}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x-1)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5(5x-1)^{6}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(5x-1)^{6}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387d85df-b839-5837-89b9-5e4bb4daa073" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Negative Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7360ad74-6fe9-5223-97a8-69c435c43bc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6(2x+3)^{6}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255954} {:answer/id #uuid "f41518ea-84c4-5d8e-ae72-344931e302ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255955} {:answer/id #uuid "0adbf264-1352-5ca3-8fc9-1b3771272720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255956} {:answer/id #uuid "8827db20-b595-5791-af13-4ddaaf6bfd7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{16(2x+3)^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255957} {:answer/id #uuid "4084494f-1e1b-5c69-85d8-c427b5db14c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(2x+3)^{8}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f41518ea-84c4-5d8e-ae72-344931e302ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255955} :answer-field/id #uuid "a721bb6b-7934-58b1-8fab-de1e1d92a61e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255953}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bdd59737-ae15-573f-9634-0d492e32540a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113512" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{1}{(2x+3)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (2x+3)^{-7}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2x+3.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+3)^{-7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{-7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{-7}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{6}){u}^{-6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12{u}^{6}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{12(2x+3)^{6}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(2x+3)^{-6}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot (-6)\\cdot (2x+3)^{-7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+3)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(2x+3)^{7}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(2x+3)^{7}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387d85df-b839-5837-89b9-5e4bb4daa073" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Negative Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0462011-84bf-59ae-8649-365326a6d481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20(9-5x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255961} {:answer/id #uuid "89259f28-d96f-5e00-9005-829562f4be25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255962} {:answer/id #uuid "0726c688-5052-50ce-9edd-ad69b0848c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255963} {:answer/id #uuid "958e66aa-520e-5e84-be2e-e1cb143515bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255964} {:answer/id #uuid "110e9da5-7e4d-5325-9512-b0772dba01fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "958e66aa-520e-5e84-be2e-e1cb143515bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255964} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccdca3b1-2f84-5f84-8686-232cb799c22e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255960}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d34fadec-e1db-5f0e-b3fb-64f3326f1376" :question/math-academy-id "q-113517" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{(9-5x)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (9-5x)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=9-5x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (9-5x)^{-3}\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{-3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}){u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10{u}^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{10(9-5x)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(9-5x)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot (-2)(9-5x)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9-5x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}(9-5x)^{-3}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =(9-5x)^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(9-5x)}^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Fractional Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0236b725-105a-51b3-aa66-6629019d32a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255968} {:answer/id #uuid "ca277357-5421-5c57-96d4-bedc46d2f129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{5x+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255969} {:answer/id #uuid "4ddd09ed-859e-5506-bb5a-b3d8d30518cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{5x+1}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255970} {:answer/id #uuid "1356d90a-4d36-5738-a84e-51683ecaa86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255971} {:answer/id #uuid "1cd51266-2143-558a-b3b1-b5f1332b1305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1356d90a-4d36-5738-a84e-51683ecaa86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255971} :answer-field/id #uuid "50bbb8e2-65a8-533f-9ee1-15004c873ce2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255967}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "457b9ae0-36a8-577c-85ad-8057dc66fc9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-12498" :question/problem "$\\int \\sqrt{5x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (5x+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=5x+1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5x+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{1/2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}{u}^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}(5x+1)^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}+C] & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\sqrt{(5x+1)^{3}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(5x+1)^{3/2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(5x+1)^{1/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x+1)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(5x+1)^{1/2}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =(5x+1)^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5x+1}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Fractional Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bae468b8-a0be-5f43-8752-0da783a87487" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{20}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255975} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4a1436-d46b-5256-a88f-1c4ecc99fa91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{20}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255976} {:answer/id #uuid "987cbf2f-7fa9-5128-b1f4-43d94fa392bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255977} {:answer/id #uuid "9d85911a-7b92-50f7-90f7-32793bcd92bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255978} {:answer/id #uuid "2d3629dc-e170-57de-9d13-daace66ab579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bae468b8-a0be-5f43-8752-0da783a87487" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{20}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255975} :answer-field/id #uuid "023632fb-f67b-5aeb-992d-21184bbbe8b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255974}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0627661-1702-5ba3-b036-6efedf7ba0f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-17019" :question/problem "Calculate the integral\n$\\int \\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (3-4x)^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we let  $u=3-4x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3-4x)^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{2/3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5/3}{u}^{5/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}{u}^{5/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{20}{u}^{5/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{20}(3-4x)^{5/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{20}\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{5}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{3}{20}(3-4x)^{5/3}+C] & =-\\frac{3}{20}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(3-4x)^{5/3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{20}\\cdot \\frac{5}{3}(3-4x)^{2/3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3-4x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(3-4x)^{3/2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =(3-4x)^{3/2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{(3-4x)^{2}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Fractional Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8be0f720-9b24-5463-8644-62fdf3a5fc13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063173} {:answer/id #uuid "97aade93-135e-551c-a502-cbfd409ab108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{4y - 1} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063174} {:answer/id #uuid "ad134924-29f6-57ac-861c-e86a6ac5d741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063175} {:answer/id #uuid "c94b14ad-ec68-5f9f-9a09-be0bc0cc4024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063176} {:answer/id #uuid "f68959d6-0379-5187-ba8a-5695f9810a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad134924-29f6-57ac-861c-e86a6ac5d741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063175} :answer-field/id #uuid "85340826-8abf-586a-8f9f-3e28f87917d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063172}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c4056b3-c70d-593e-9370-73ee76b66f6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49391" :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}dy$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (4y-1)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=4y-1.$ Then differentiating with respect to $y$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}y=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4y-1)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(1/2)}{u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{4}\\cdot {u}^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4y-1)^{1/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4y-1}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[\\frac{\\sqrt{4y-1}}{2}+C] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[\\sqrt{4y-1}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}[(4y-1)^{1/2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(4y-1)^{-1/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(4y-1)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(4y-1)^{-1/2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4y-1}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Fractional Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea7d49c9-4759-5795-8740-a64336576900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255982} {:answer/id #uuid "041652d2-599f-5a59-bde6-5a1c1b0b808e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{7}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255983} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b86588-d1c5-57a3-8324-3b7fdc7643f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255984} {:answer/id #uuid "88937ad0-3ec1-5048-913e-a8fe44545a9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3\\sqrt[4]{1-5s}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255985} {:answer/id #uuid "f991f033-2887-5df7-b463-f1e0d7646b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea7d49c9-4759-5795-8740-a64336576900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255982} :answer-field/id #uuid "57925569-9f2a-5c3b-9372-ee2440557bd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255981}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4273b028-6380-56df-90b6-0dc14e74ee2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49393" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{(3-5s)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}s=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (3-5s)^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNow, we let  $u=3-5s.$ Then differentiating with respect to $s$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}s}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}s=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3-5s)^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}s & =\\int {u}^{-2/3}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {u}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1/3}{u}^{1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{u}^{1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}(3-5s)^{1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[-\\frac{3}{5}\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}+C] & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[\\sqrt[3]{3-5s}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}[(3-5s)^{1/3}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}(3-5s)^{-2/3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(3-5s)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}(3-5s)^{-2/3}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =(3-5s)^{-2/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{(3-5s)^{2}}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Fractional Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6974fcbd-fc66-5d4d-8798-2dc3ffbd4389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{11}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255989} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6e8082-7b80-51ac-9c78-f7c8cc246f61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255990} {:answer/id #uuid "8e6a96a9-9b9b-5cba-9a65-3490ba742380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255991} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a4ed23-2b46-5648-850c-91c8d7211a8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{9}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255992} {:answer/id #uuid "55a4f1f0-0762-5f16-a317-ca6180888bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{9}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6974fcbd-fc66-5d4d-8798-2dc3ffbd4389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{11}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255989} :answer-field/id #uuid "afb0006f-3f23-56ee-88f7-28fbc4472d13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255988}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61d8dd43-99c6-5162-9111-9fc96bb88dcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-49439" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int \\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (x-100)^{7/4}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we let  $u=x-100.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $u$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x-100)^{7/4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{7/4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{11/4}}{11/4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{11}(x-100)^{11/4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{11}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{4}{11}\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}+C] & =\\frac{4}{11}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{11}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{11}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(x-100)^{11/4}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{11}\\cdot \\frac{11}{4}(x-100)^{7/4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x-100)+0 \\\\  & =(x-100)^{7/4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\sqrt[4]{(x-100)^{7}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255994 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b47545-fdf1-5e6a-b0bb-bbbecb8067cc" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Positive Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f8ec8ec-677b-58b6-ae42-62ec81f9bfe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255996} {:answer/id #uuid "2fa9061c-018a-502b-8f17-0c8208d11c99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255997} {:answer/id #uuid "805518e3-d5f7-5f73-8953-259d06975795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255998} {:answer/id #uuid "505cc434-c74e-5dc4-8e46-3477df12efd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255999} {:answer/id #uuid "5a9db785-6fbb-5738-b4e8-df9a63e710a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f8ec8ec-677b-58b6-ae42-62ec81f9bfe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(7-2x)^{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255996} :answer-field/id #uuid "f56c58ed-d97c-51ce-a838-cbc7115d5792" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255995}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c75bb9c-44e2-5f73-9a68-3c296ae237a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72424" :question/problem "$\\int 16(7-2x)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=7-2x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 16(7-2x)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 16{u}^{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\int {u}^{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\int {u}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{8}}{8}+C \\\\  & =-{u}^{8}+C \\\\  & =-(7-2x)^{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-(7-2x)^{8}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(7-2x)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-8(7-2x)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-2x)+0 \\\\  & =-8(7-2x)^{7}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =16(7-2x)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387d85df-b839-5837-89b9-5e4bb4daa073" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Negative Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "debbb027-6e7f-5907-82a3-fcdf1dfbc424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256003} {:answer/id #uuid "0a57e3fb-2bf3-565e-8b71-f170fbd5a13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256004} {:answer/id #uuid "70b95a79-24f0-56c3-9c4e-41afedf8910b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256005} {:answer/id #uuid "a7ce7760-15b6-5db1-b09f-6d2f2ccede52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256006} {:answer/id #uuid "0489fd82-f146-57d2-ab56-a6315be6a3b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0489fd82-f146-57d2-ab56-a6315be6a3b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256007} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcb36960-42db-5176-ab59-fa02936d8e91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256002}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7bfa495-1b68-5727-9e29-0eace5070a84" :question/math-academy-id "q-72431" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{4}{(8-x)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 4(8-x)^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=8-x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4(8-x)^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int {u}^{-5}\\cdot (-1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)\\int {u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\int {u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{(-4)}{u}^{-4}+C \\\\  & =(8-x)^{-4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{1}{(8-x)^{4}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(8-x)^{-4}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =(-4)(8-x)^{-5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8-x)+0 \\\\  & =(-4)(8-x)^{-5}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4(8-x)^{-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(8-x)^{5}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
